June 6, 2026
- Conducted initial brainstorming and concept development.
- Established the vision for Orbii, a human-mimicking robotic platform inspired by the "Rocky" robot featured in Project Hail Mary.
- Defined preliminary project objectives and functionality requirements.

June 7 - June 14, 2026
- Developed the first CAD model for the Orbii.
- Designed initial electronic schematics and hardware architecture.
- Prepared and completed the Thompson Innovation Fund (TIF) application package, including project description, technical design overview, and BOM.

June 15, 2026
- Submitted TIF application.

June 19, 2026
- TIF application approved.
- ordered required components and prototyping materials.

July 8, 2026
- Received initial shipment of project materials.

July 18, 2026
- Successfully integrated MediaPipe pose-tracking software with two servo motors.
- Demonstrated real-time movement of two servos based on the measured angle between the right shoulder and right elbow.
- Validated feasibility of motion replication for future full-body implementation and realized that it is hard to capture the leg movement in most of the angle from the orbii camera.
- decided to make the orbii move forward, backward, left right based on the particular gesture.

July 20, 2026
- 3D printing of Orbii body has been initiated.
- thoughout the printing, identified structural weaknesses caused by insufficient wall thickness in the initial design.
- Revised CAD design and increased wall thickness to improve manufacturability and mechanical integrity.
- Initiated reprinting of modified components and went successful

